From: lazy-jubei
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: expose the containing window for accessibility hits

Blank client areas resolve to WineWindow itself. Cocoa normally omits AXWindow
from a window, so automation clients cannot resolve the containing window for
that hit. Return the window itself through the standard accessibility getter.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -1061,6 +1061,13 @@
     @synthesize usePerPixelAlpha;
     @synthesize himc, commandDone;
     @synthesize contentViewMaskLayer;
+
+    /* A hit on blank Wine content resolves directly to this window.  Keep the
+       containing-window attribute available to accessibility controllers. */
+    - (id) accessibilityWindow
+    {
+        return self;
+    }
 
     + (WineWindow*) createWindowWithFeatures:(const struct macdrv_window_features*)wf
                                  windowFrame:(NSRect)window_frame
